{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"830","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Perpetual Motion Machine"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Developer Petr thinks that he invented a perpetual motion machine. Namely, he has a lot of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"elements"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", which work in the following way."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each element has one controller that can be set to any non-negative real value. If a controller is set on some value "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":", then the controller consumes "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x2"},{"kind":"text","text":" energy units per second. At the same time, any two elements connected by a wire produce "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y·z"},{"kind":"text","text":" energy units per second, where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"z"},{"kind":"text","text":" are the values set on their controllers."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Petr has only a limited number of wires, so he has already built some scheme of elements and wires, and is now interested if it's possible to set the controllers in such a way that the system produces "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"at least as much"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" power as it consumes, and at least one controller is set on the value different from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":". Help him check this, and if it's possible, find the required "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"integer"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" values that should be set."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that if there exist controllers' settings satisfying the above conditions, then there exist required integer values not greater than "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"106"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are several (at least one) test cases in the input. The first line contains single integer — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There is an empty line before each test case. The first line of test case contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 105"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ m ≤ 105"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of elements in the scheme and the number of wires."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After that, "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines follow, each of them contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ a, b ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":") — two elements connected by a wire. No element is connected with itself, no two elements are connected by more than one wire."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and the sum of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" over all test cases do not exceed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"105"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For hacks"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" you can only use tests with one test case."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print answer for each test case."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if it's possible to set the controllers in such a way that the consumed power is not greater than the power produced, and the required values on the next line. The settings should be integers from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"106"},{"kind":"text","text":", inclusive, and at least one value should be different from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":". If there are multiple answers, print any of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If it's not possible to set the controllers in the required way, print one line \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n \n4 4\n1 2\n2 3\n3 4\n4 2\n \n3 2\n2 3\n3 1\n \n4 6\n1 2\n3 4\n4 2\n1 4\n1 3\n3 2\n \n10 9\n2 1\n3 2\n5 2\n6 2\n2 7\n2 8\n2 9\n2 10\n4 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"YES\n1 2 2 1\nNO\nYES\n1 1 1 1\nYES\n1 5 1 1 1 1 1 1 1 1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example it's possible to set the controllers in the required way, for example, in the following way: set "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" on the first element, set "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" on the second and on the third, set "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" on the fourth. The consumed power is then equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"12 + 22 + 22 + 12 = 10"},{"kind":"text","text":" energy units per second, the produced power is equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1·2 + 2·2 + 2·1 + 2·1 = 10"},{"kind":"text","text":" energy units per second. Thus the answer is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case it's not possible to set the controllers in the required way. For example, if we set all controllers to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0.5"},{"kind":"text","text":", then the consumed powers equals "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0.75"},{"kind":"text","text":" energy units per second, while produced power equals "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0.5"},{"kind":"text","text":" energy units per second."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"830E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/830/problem/E"}